---
title: Crown Roast of Lamb
servings: 4
prepTime: 45 mins
cookTime: 100 mins
Rating: 10/10
source: https://www.seriouseats.com/crown-roast-of-lamb-recipe-11709766
tags: Lamb, Show-Stopper
---

Preheat oven to 200°F and position oven rack low enough to fit crown roast in oven.
Generously season @crown roast of lamb{4%lb} all over with @Kosher salt{} and @pepper.

Place roast on a rack set in a rimmed baking sheet and roast until lamb registers
115°F on an instant-read thermometer inserted into center of loin, ~{1-1.5%hours}.

When lamb reaches 115°F (46°C), remove from oven.
Increase oven to highest possible temperature (broil setting on some ovens, or about 500°F)
and allow to heat fully.

Cover lamb rib bones with foil.
Roast lamb, checking temperature every ~{5%minutes} and then more frequently as it
approaches doneness, until lamb is browned and an instant-read thermometer inserted
into thickest part of lamb registers 125 to 130°F for medium-rare,
or 130 to 135°F for medium, about ~{10%minutes}.
Let lamb rest for 15 minutes.

To carve lamb, slice lamb between rib bones into chops. Serve with red wine au jus.

